INSERT INTO `Comment` VALUES (7593,'Sent a PR based on some initial benchmarking. Turns out that how threading is handled in a stream becomes very important in the overall throughput. Initial ingestion benchmarking shows the reactor-syslog module can pull in messages at a rate of about [edit: tweaked some things to get a more conservative approach to line handling which lowers overall throughput] 400k/sec on a 2013 MacBook Pro.\n\nKeep in mind that end to end throughput will be significantly lower than the ingestion micro-benchmark. Benchmarks of syslog to HDFS tests yield about 700k/sec (end to end) without the overhead of XD.','\"Sent a PR based on some initial benchmarking. Turns out that how threading is handled in a stream becomes very important in the overall throughput. Initial ingestion benchmarking shows the reactor-syslog module can pull in messages at a rate of about [edit: tweaked some things to get a more conservative approach to line handling which lowers overall throughput] 400k/sec on a 2013 MacBook Pro.  Keep in mind that end to end throughput will be significantly lower than the ingestion micro-benchmark. Benchmarks of syslog to HDFS tests yield about 700k/sec (end to end) without the overhead of XD.\"','','2013-09-24 11:51:38',151,2934);
INSERT INTO `Comment` VALUES (7594,'What is the rate with the original syslog adapter in XD?','\"What is the rate with the original syslog adapter in XD?\"','','2013-09-24 14:00:59',72,2934);
INSERT INTO `Comment` VALUES (7595,'I was getting around 29k/sec.','\"I was getting around 29k/sec.\"','','2013-09-24 14:02:20',151,2934);
INSERT INTO `Comment` VALUES (7596,'This was syslog-x | counter?','\"This was syslog-x | counter?\"','','2013-09-24 14:59:03',72,2934);
INSERT INTO `Comment` VALUES (7597,'I created two streams to test. For the reactor-syslog stuff (which uses the syslog standard port of 5140):\n\n{{stream create --name syslog --definition \"reactor-syslog | counter --name=msgCount\"}}\n\nand for the earlier syslog-tcp stuff (which uses a default port of 11111):\n\n{{stream create --name syslogtcp --definition \"syslog-tcp | counter --name=tcpMsgCount\"}}\n\nI have an \"external server\" test in the Reactor TCP module that I use to test syslog servers. I can adjust the number of messages sent and the number of sending threads that way.','\"I created two streams to test. For the reactor-syslog stuff (which uses the syslog standard port of 5140):  {{stream create --name syslog --definition \"\"reactor-syslog | counter --name=msgCount\"\"}}  and for the earlier syslog-tcp stuff (which uses a default port of 11111):  {{stream create --name syslogtcp --definition \"\"syslog-tcp | counter --name=tcpMsgCount\"\"}}  I have an \"\"external server\"\" test in the Reactor TCP module that I use to test syslog servers. I can adjust the number of messages sent and the number of sending threads that way.\"','','2013-09-24 15:30:57',151,2934);
INSERT INTO `Comment` VALUES (7598,'Thanks, can you also point me to the \'external server\' test you mention as I think it would be useful for me to try out and also useful as part of a larger distributed system test for XD.','\"Thanks, can you also point me to the \'external server\' test you mention as I think it would be useful for me to try out and also useful as part of a larger distributed system test for XD.\"','','2013-09-24 21:11:42',72,2934);
INSERT INTO `Comment` VALUES (7599,'The test is here: \n\nhttps://github.com/reactor/reactor/blob/master/reactor-tcp/src/test/java/reactor/tcp/syslog/SyslogTcpServerTests.java#L187\n\nI just run that test individually from the IDE (and change the port number to match what I\'m testing of course). Other parameters are defined at the top of the class (msg count and threads).\n','\"The test is here:   https://github.com/reactor/reactor/blob/master/reactor-tcp/src/test/java/reactor/tcp/syslog/SyslogTcpServerTests.java#L187  I just run that test individually from the IDE (and change the port number to match what I\'m testing of course). Other parameters are defined at the top of the class (msg count and threads). \"','','2013-09-30 10:03:44',72,2934);
INSERT INTO `Comment` VALUES (7600,'Cool, I was able to reproduce the functionality.','\"Cool, I was able to reproduce the functionality.\"','','2013-09-30 16:48:34',72,2934);
