:37:24.659Z | TRACE  | done with plugin [Error: titanium exited with non-zero exit code (1)]  2016-04-20T13:37:25.209Z | ERROR  | Error: titanium exited with non-zero exit code (1)      at ChildProcess.<anonymous> (C:\\Users\\jorgenbuder\\.<USER>install\\5.2.2\\package\\node_modules\\appc-cli-titanium  \\plugins\\new.js:204:21)      at ChildProcess.emit (events.js:110:17)      at Process.ChildProcess._handle.onexit (child_process.js:1074:12)  2016-04-20T13:37:25.224Z | TRACE  | Sending exit signal to titanium <USER>  1188  PS Z:\\Users\\jorgenbuder\\Documents\\<USER>Studio_Workspace>\"','','2016-04-20 13:39:14',166486,406746);
INSERT INTO `Comment` VALUES (1324545,'One other thing is that looking at the last lines it seems there are files copied over to the target but there is nothing there not even a folder..','\"One other thing is that looking at the last lines it seems there are files copied over to the target but there is nothing there not even a folder..\"','','2016-04-20 13:40:33',166486,406746);
INSERT INTO `Comment` VALUES (1324546,'Hi\r\n\r\nI think I managed:\r\n\r\nDo not use appc to create module do this instead:\r\n\r\nti create -p windows -t module --wp-sdk 8.1\r\n\r\nthen build with \r\n\r\nti build -p windows -T ws-local\r\n\r\nthis will create a project with the background service you made and also builds a valid zip file with 235 Kbytes or so, now I have to test it with the main app .\r\n\r\nI do not know why but the appc create module does not work\r\n\r\n(I use the 5.4.0  20160420 SDK)\r\n\r\ndoes this help ?\r\n\r\n','\"Hi    I think I managed:    Do not use appc to create module do this instead:    ti create -p windows -t module --wp-sdk 8.1    then build with     ti build -p windows -T ws-local    this will create a project with the background service you made and also builds a valid zip file with 235 Kbytes or so, now I have to test it with the main app .    I do not know why but the appc create module does not work    (I use the 5.4.0  20160420 SDK)    does this help ?    \"','','2016-04-20 13:50:38',166486,406746);
INSERT INTO `Comment` VALUES (1324547,'I think I\'m close. Please wait for the update I will make tomorrow.','\"I think I\'m close. Please wait for the update I will make tomorrow.\"','','2016-04-20 13:50:56',166083,406746);
INSERT INTO `Comment` VALUES (1324548,'Oh yes it does help!! Thanks :)','\"Oh yes it does help!! Thanks :)\"','','2016-04-20 13:51:49',166083,406746);
INSERT INTO `Comment` VALUES (1324549,'Problem I have then is that I cannot use my old module and just add the class you made in the cpp and hpp file it seems the only way to use the same module as before is to make a new one (do not know if I can use the same name). \r\n\r\nI do not yet have a confirmation that this will work all the way with the background service but I think maybe I can now make a module that should be able to expose the background service task to the app..\r\n\r\nUnfortunately I have to leave now, it must be late with you too... I think I can work with this unless you see any obvious problem creating the module like so??\r\n\r\nI will get back to you when I tested to use this new module as background task function..\r\n\r\nI will be back in a few hours but I guess I will see you tomorrow...\r\n\r\nbye','\"Problem I have then is that I cannot use my old module and just add the class you made in the cpp and hpp file it seems the only way to use the same module as before is to make a new one (do not know if I can use the same name).     I do not yet have a confirmation that this will work all the way with the background service but I think maybe I can now make a module that should be able to expose the background service task to the app..    Unfortunately I have to leave now, it must be late with you too... I think I can work with this unless you see any obvious problem creating the module like so??    I will get back to you when I tested to use this new module as background task function..    I will be back in a few hours but I guess I will see you tomorrow...    bye\"','','2016-04-20 13:54:46',166486,406746);
INSERT INTO `Comment` VALUES (1324550,'Should be fixed by TIMOB-23248','\"Should be fixed by TIMOB-23248\"','','2016-04-22 07:35:21',166083,406746);
INSERT INTO `Comment` VALUES (1324551,'Hi\r\n\r\nSo since this is resolved now, it means we have this in the mighty build? Can you tell me how I can see for my self which merges and tickets go into what nightly build? Is there a release list for each nightly build? I have tried the decodeNumber and when it did not work you said it was nto yet in, can I have a insight in how I can resolve this myself and not take up your time? \r\n\r\nBut this ticket should be in 20160422 nightly build correct?','\"Hi    So since this is resolved now, it means we have this in the mighty build? Can you tell me how I can see for my self which merges and tickets go into what nightly build? Is there a release list for each nightly build? I have tried the decodeNumber and when it did not work you said it was nto yet in, can I have a insight in how I can resolve this myself and not take up your time?     But this ticket should be in 20160422 nightly build correct?\"','','2016-04-22 07:41:19',166486,406746);
INSERT INTO `Comment` VALUES (1324552,'I\'m not very sure exactly when nightly build is invoked. I usually check [<USER>Nightly Build Server|http://builds.<USER>com/#master], and check its timestamp. \r\n','\"I\'m not very sure exactly when nightly build is invoked. I usually check [<USER>Nightly Build Server|http://builds.<USER>com/#master], and check its timestamp.   \"','','2016-04-22 07:53:48',166083,406746);
INSERT INTO `Comment` VALUES (1324553,'Did you solve this for Win 10 as well, we are now trying your appc new command line but are getting same type of error there, the system complains about not having all SDK installed, while we can build our app to emulator (at least) this should not be a problem. Please respond..\r\n\r\nappc new -n test -id com.ps --wp-sdk 8.1\r\n\r\nthis does not work, \r\n\r\nrequieing Windows 10 SDK and Windows Store SDK, why is this a problem ?\r\n\r\nRunning SDK 0428 5.4.0\r\n\r\n','\"Did you solve this for Win 10 as well, we are now trying your appc new command line but are getting same type of error there, the system complains about not having all SDK installed, while we can build our app to emulator (at least) this should not be a problem. Please respond..    appc new -n test -id com.ps --wp-sdk 8.1    this does not work,     requieing Windows 10 SDK and Windows Store SDK, why is this a problem ?    Running SDK 0428 5.4.0    \"','','2016-05-04 07:43:00',166486,406746);
INSERT INTO `Comment` VALUES (1324554,'It sounds like to me it needs Windows Phone 8.1 SDK too for you since you are specifying {{wp-sdk 8.1}} ?  Just in case, how about specifying {{sdk}} to make sure to use latest sdk: {{appc new -n TIMOB23246 --id com.appc.TIMOB23246 --wp-sdk 8.1 --sdk 5.4.0.v20160504215815}}','\"It sounds like to me it needs Windows Phone 8.1 SDK too for you since you are specifying {{wp-sdk 8.1}} ?  Just in case, how about specifying {{sdk}} to make sure to use latest sdk: {{appc new -n TIMOB23246 --id com.appc.TIMOB23246 --wp-sdk 8.1 --sdk 5.4.0.v20160504215815}}\"','','2016-05-05 07:34:32',166083,406746);
INSERT INTO `Comment` VALUES (1324555,'Hi\r\n\r\nDid not see this comment until now, will take a look at it however we have a bigger problem. A native module cannot be used in SDKs later than 0420, any native module crashes the app on the device making it impossible for me to test your background service on device, I have struggled with this now. I have confirmed that if I use the latest SDK 20160511 I can build and deploy the app ONLY if I remove the native module, and this worked in the 20160420 SDK I used before. This is critical, please reopen and investigate.. thanks','\"Hi    Did not see this comment until now, will take a look at it however we have a bigger problem. A native module cannot be used in SDKs later than 0420, any native module crashes the app on the device making it impossible for me to test your background service on device, I have struggled with this now. I have confirmed that if I use the latest SDK 20160511 I can build and deploy the app ONLY if I remove the native module, and this worked in the 20160420 SDK I used before. This is critical, please reopen and investigate.. thanks\"','','2016-05-12 12:01:16',166486,406746);
INSERT INTO `Comment` VALUES (1324556,'Re-opening as per user comment...','\"Re-opening as per user comment...\"','','2016-05-23 14:13:52',166009,406746);
INSERT INTO `Comment` VALUES (1324557,'Closing this for now, because this ticket is originally created to describe \"module project is not created\" that can be marked as fixed. I think we want to be more specific to the case, I will create new ticket that is more specific to actual issue that something like \"module does not work\" or \"Windows module crashes\" according to the report.','\"Closing this for now, because this ticket is originally created to describe \"\"module project is not created\"\" that can be marked as fixed. I think we want to be more specific to the case, I will create new ticket that is more specific to actual issue that something like \"\"module does not work\"\" or \"\"Windows module crashes\"\" according to the report.\"','','2016-05-27 03:40:21',166083,406746);
INSERT INTO `Comment` VALUES (1324558,'[~<USER> I tried native module on the the latest 5.3.0.v20160523083840 and 5.4.0.v20160530173143 but I was not able to reproduce crash you described. Could you create new ticket for this rather than adding comments on this ticket, to track the issue? It would be very welcome if you include full CLI command and output you executed and hopefully source code when needed.\r\n\r\nFYI what I did was to create/build module using following CLI commands.\r\n\r\nFor 5_3_X: \r\n{code}\r\n> appc new -n TIMOB23246 --id com.appc.TIMOB23246 --sdk 5.3.0.v20160523083840\r\n> cd TIMOB23246/windows\r\n> ti build -p windows --sdk 5.3.0.v20160523083840 --build-only\r\n{code}\r\n\r\nFor 5_4_X:\r\n{code}\r\n> appc new -n TIMOB23246X54 --id com.appc.TIMOB23246X54 --sdk 5.4.0.v20160530173143\r\n> cd TIMOB23246X54/windows\r\n> ti build -p windows --sdk 5.4.0.v20160530173143 --build-only\r\n{code}\r\n\r\nAnd then in app.js:\r\n\r\n{code}\r\n﻿var TIMOB23246 = require(\'com.appc.TIMOB23246\');\r\nvar TIMOB23246X54 = require(\'com.appc.TIMOB23246X54\');\r\n\r\nTi.API.info(typeof TIMOB23246);\r\nTi.API.info(typeof TIMOB23246X54);\r\n{code}\r\n','\"[~<USER> I tried native module on the the latest 5.3.0.v20160523083840 and 5.4.0.v20160530173143 but I was not able to reproduce crash you described. Could you create new ticket for this rather than adding comments on this ticket, to track the issue? It would be very welcome if you include full CLI command and output you executed and hopefully source code when needed.    FYI what I did was to create/build module using following CLI commands.    For 5_3_X:       For 5_4_X:      And then in app.js:      \"','\"  > appc new -n TIMOB23246 --id com.appc.TIMOB23246 --sdk 5.3.0.v20160523083840  > cd TIMOB23246/windows  > ti build -p windows --sdk 5.3.0.v20160523083840 --build-only    > appc new -n TIMOB23246X54 --id com.appc.TIMOB23246X54 --sdk 5.4.0.v20160530173143  > cd TIMOB23246X54/windows  > ti build -p windows --sdk 5.4.0.v20160530173143 --build-only    ﻿var TIMOB23246 = require(\'com.appc.TIMOB23246\');  var TIMOB23246X54 = require(\'com.appc.TIMOB23246X54\');    Ti.API.info(typeof TIMOB23246);  Ti.API.info(typeof TIMOB23246X54);  \"','2016-05-31 06:21:23',166083,406746);
INSERT INTO `Comment` VALUES (1324559,'Reopening ticket:\r\n\r\nIn the following circumstances module creation will fail:\r\n\r\n* A machine that has Visual Studio installed, Universal App Development tools installed, Windows Phone 8.0/8.1 tools **not** installed\r\n{code}\r\n[INFO]  Generating WindowsPhone ARM project\r\n[INFO]  Generating solution under vsbuild directory to avoid path length issues.\r\n..\r\n[WARN]  CMake Error at CMakeLists.txt:20 (project):\r\n  A Windows Phone component with CMake requires both the Windows Desktop SDK\r\n  as well as the Windows Phone \'8.1\' SDK.  Please make sure that you have\r\n  both installed\r\n[INFO]  -- Configuring incomplete, errors occurred!\r\nSee also \"C:/Users/tester/.titanium/vsbuild/windmodule/WindowsPhone.ARM/CMakeFil\r\nes/CMakeOutput.log\".\r\n{code}\r\n\r\nI believe if a check is placed to ensure that 8.1 SDK is installed before running CMake [here|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile_windows/blob/0b4070a5dbe8ccf88e4215fac186147cf00a65ad/templates/module/default/hooks/windows-module.js#L74] then this error will not be thrown, same for [line 78| https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile_windows/blob/0b4070a5dbe8ccf88e4215fac186147cf00a65ad/templates/module/default/hooks/windows-module.js#L78] and [82|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile_windows/blob/0b4070a5dbe8ccf88e4215fac186147cf00a65ad/templates/module/default/hooks/windows-module.js#L82]\r\n\r\nAdditionally based off the above, in the following circumstance I believe that the <USER>will error out. I am setting up a machine to confirm this currently\r\n\r\n* A Windows 10 machine that has Visual Studio installed, Universal App Development tools not installed, Windows Phone 8.0/8.1 tools installed and is using a version of node >0.12.7\r\n\r\nSimilar to the above, rather than check for Windows 10 [here|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile_windows/blob/0b4070a5dbe8ccf88e4215fac186147cf00a65ad/templates/module/default/hooks/windows-module.js#L85] the presence of Windows 10 SDKs should be checked. This would also stop the use of os.release() which currently require Studio to upgrade the version of node it installs due to\r\n\r\n*NOTES*\r\n\r\nI have modified the code and uploaded as a [gist here|https://gist.github.com/eharrisappcel/2480e5179c32b1cd02ccd8594887ab4b] using the shown above no longer occurs in the same configuration\r\n\r\n{code}\r\nC:\\Users\\tester\\Documents\\<USER>Studio_Workspace>ti create -p windows -n winmodule --id win.module --force\r\nTitanium Command-Line Interface, CLI version 5.0.9, Titanium SDK version 5.4.0.v20160627224205\r\nCopyright (c) 2012-2015, <USER> Inc.  All Rights Reserved.\r\n\r\nPlease report bugs to http://jira.<USER>org/\r\n\r\nWhat type of project would you like to create?\r\n 1)  Titanium App\r\n 2)  Titanium Module\r\nSelect a type by number or name [app]: 2\r\n\r\nDirectory to place project [.]:\r\n\r\n[INFO]  Creating module project\r\n[INFO]  Template directory: C:\\ProgramData\\Titanium\\mobilesdk\\win32\\5.4.0.v20160627224205\\templates\\module\\default\r\n[DEBUG] Copying C:\\ProgramData\\Titanium\\mobilesdk\\win32\\5.4.0.v20160627224205\\templates\\module\\default\\template\\assets\\README.ejs => C:\\Users\\tester\\Docume\r\n[DEBUG] Copying C:\\ProgramData\\Titanium\\mobilesdk\\win32\\5.4.0.v20160627224205\\templates\\module\\default\\template\\documentation\\index.md.ejs => C:\\Users\\test\r\n[DEBUG] Copying C:\\ProgramData\\Titanium\\mobilesdk\\win32\\5.4.0.v20160627224205\\templates\\module\\default\\template\\example\\app.js.ejs => C:\\Users\\tester\\Docum\r\n[DEBUG] Copying C:\\ProgramData\\Titanium\\mobilesdk\\win32\\5.4.0.v20160627224205\\templates\\module\\default\\template\\LICENSE => C:\\Users\\tester\\Documents\\Appcel\r\n[DEBUG] Copying C:\\ProgramData\\Titanium\\mobilesdk\\win32\\5.4.0.v20160627224205\\templates\\module\\default\\template\\README.ejs => C:\\Users\\tester\\Documents\\App\r\n[INFO]  Copying windows platform resources\r\n[DEBUG] Copying C:\\ProgramData\\Titanium\\mobilesdk\\win32\\5.4.0.v20160627224205\\windows\\templates\\module\\default\\template\\windows\\cmake\\{{moduleIdAsIdentifie\r\n[DEBUG] Copying C:\\ProgramData\\Titanium\\mobilesdk\\win32\\5.4.0.v20160627224205\\windows\\templates\\module\\default\\template\\windows\\CMakeLists.txt.ejs => C:\\Us\r\n[DEBUG] Copying C:\\ProgramData\\Titanium\\mobilesdk\\win32\\5.4.0.v20160627224205\\windows\\templates\\module\\default\\template\\windows\\include\\{{moduleIdAsIdentif\r\n[DEBUG] Copying C:\\ProgramData\\Titanium\\mobilesdk\\win32\\5.4.0.v20160627224205\\windows\\templates\\module\\default\\template\\windows\\manifest.ejs => C:\\Users\\te\r\n[DEBUG] Copying C:\\ProgramData\\Titanium\\mobilesdk\\win32\\5.4.0.v20160627224205\\windows\\templates\\module\\default\\template\\windows\\src\\{{moduleIdAsIdentifier}\r\n[DEBUG] Copying C:\\ProgramData\\Titanium\\mobilesdk\\win32\\5.4.0.v20160627224205\\windows\\templates\\module\\default\\template\\windows\\test\\CMakeLists.txt.ejs =>\r\n[DEBUG] Copying C:\\ProgramData\\Titanium\\mobilesdk\\win32\\5.4.0.v20160627224205\\windows\\templates\\module\\default\\template\\windows\\timodule.xml => C:\\Users\\te\r\n[INFO]  Copying CMake package finders\r\n[INFO]  Skipping WindowsPhone ARM project as Windows 8.1 SDK is not installed\r\n[INFO]  Skipping WindowsPhone Win32 project as Windows 8.1 SDK is not installed\r\n[INFO]  Skipping WindowsStore Win3 project as Windows 8.1 SDK is not installed\r\n[INFO]  Generating Windows 10 Win32 project\r\n[INFO]  Generating solution under vsbuild directory to avoid path length issues...\r\n[INFO]  -- The C compiler identification is MSVC 19.0.24210.0\r\n[INFO]  -- The CXX compiler identification is MSVC 19.0.24210.0\r\n[INFO]  -- Check for working C compiler using: Visual Studio 14 2015\r\n[INFO]  -- Check for working C compiler using: Visual Studio 14 2015 -- works\r\n[INFO]  -- Detecting C compiler ABI info\r\n[INFO]  -- Detecting C compiler ABI info - done\r\n[INFO