ing done\r\n[INFO]  -- Build files have been written to: C:/Users/tester/.titanium/vsbuild/winmodule/Windows10.ARM\r\n[INFO]  Copying solution back to module from temp directory...\r\n[INFO]  Project created successfully in 27s 574ms\r\n{code}','\"Reopening ticket:    In the following circumstances module creation will fail:    * A machine that has Visual Studio installed, Universal App Development tools installed, Windows Phone 8.0/8.1 tools **not** installed      I believe if a check is placed to ensure that 8.1 SDK is installed before running CMake [here|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile_windows/blob/0b4070a5dbe8ccf88e4215fac186147cf00a65ad/templates/module/default/hooks/windows-module.js#L74] then this error will not be thrown, same for [line 78| https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile_windows/blob/0b4070a5dbe8ccf88e4215fac186147cf00a65ad/templates/module/default/hooks/windows-module.js#L78] and [82|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile_windows/blob/0b4070a5dbe8ccf88e4215fac186147cf00a65ad/templates/module/default/hooks/windows-module.js#L82]    Additionally based off the above, in the following circumstance I believe that the <USER>will error out. I am setting up a machine to confirm this currently    * A Windows 10 machine that has Visual Studio installed, Universal App Development tools not installed, Windows Phone 8.0/8.1 tools installed and is using a version of node >0.12.7    Similar to the above, rather than check for Windows 10 [here|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile_windows/blob/0b4070a5dbe8ccf88e4215fac186147cf00a65ad/templates/module/default/hooks/windows-module.js#L85] the presence of Windows 10 SDKs should be checked. This would also stop the use of os.release() which currently require Studio to upgrade the version of node it installs due to    *NOTES*    I have modified the code and uploaded as a [gist here|https://gist.github.com/eharrisappcel/2480e5179c32b1cd02ccd8594887ab4b] using the shown above no longer occurs in the same configuration    \"','\"  [INFO]  Generating WindowsPhone ARM project  [INFO]  Generating solution under vsbuild directory to avoid path length issues.  ..  [WARN]  CMake Error at CMakeLists.txt:20 (project):    A Windows Phone component with CMake requires both the Windows Desktop SDK    as well as the Windows Phone \'8.1\' SDK.  Please make sure that you have    both installed  [INFO]  -- Configuring incomplete, errors occurred!  See also \"\"C:/Users/tester/.titanium/vsbuild/windmodule/WindowsPhone.ARM/CMakeFil  es/CMakeOutput.log\"\".    C:\\Users\\tester\\Documents\\Appcelerator_Studio_Workspace>ti create -p windows -n winmodule --id win.module --force  Titanium Command-Line Interface, CLI version 5.0.9, Titanium SDK version 5.4.0.v20160627224205  Copyright (c) 2012-2015, Appcelerator, Inc.  All Rights Reserved.    Please report bugs to http://jira.appcelerator.org/    What type of project would you like to create?   1)  Titanium App   2)  Titanium Module  Select a type by number or name [app]: 2    Directory to place project [.]:    [INFO]  Creating module project  [INFO]  Template directory: C:\\ProgramData\\Titanium\\mobilesdk\\win32\\5.4.0.v20160627224205\\templates\\module\\default  [DEBUG] Copying C:\\ProgramData\\Titanium\\mobilesdk\\win32\\5.4.0.v20160627224205\\templates\\module\\default\\template\\assets\\README.ejs => C:\\Users\\tester\\Docume  [DEBUG] Copying C:\\ProgramData\\Titanium\\mobilesdk\\win32\\5.4.0.v20160627224205\\templates\\module\\default\\template\\documentation\\index.md.ejs => C:\\Users\\test  [DEBUG] Copying C:\\ProgramData\\Titanium\\mobilesdk\\win32\\5.4.0.v20160627224205\\templates\\module\\default\\template\\example\\app.js.ejs => C:\\Users\\tester\\Docum  [DEBUG] Copying C:\\ProgramData\\Titanium\\mobilesdk\\win32\\5.4.0.v20160627224205\\templates\\module\\default\\template\\LICENSE => C:\\Users\\tester\\Documents\\Appcel  [DEBUG] Copying C:\\ProgramData\\Titanium\\mobilesdk\\win32\\5.4.0.v20160627224205\\templates\\module\\default\\template\\README.ejs => C:\\Users\\tester\\Documents\\App  [INFO]  Copying windows platform resources  [DEBUG] Copying C:\\ProgramData\\Titanium\\mobilesdk\\win32\\5.4.0.v20160627224205\\windows\\templates\\module\\default\\template\\windows\\cmake\\{{moduleIdAsIdentifie  [DEBUG] Copying C:\\ProgramData\\Titanium\\mobilesdk\\win32\\5.4.0.v20160627224205\\windows\\templates\\module\\default\\template\\windows\\CMakeLists.txt.ejs => C:\\Us  [DEBUG] Copying C:\\ProgramData\\Titanium\\mobilesdk\\win32\\5.4.0.v20160627224205\\windows\\templates\\module\\default\\template\\windows\\include\\{{moduleIdAsIdentif  [DEBUG] Copying C:\\ProgramData\\Titanium\\mobilesdk\\win32\\5.4.0.v20160627224205\\windows\\templates\\module\\default\\template\\windows\\manifest.ejs => C:\\Users\\te  [DEBUG] Copying C:\\ProgramData\\Titanium\\mobilesdk\\win32\\5.4.0.v20160627224205\\windows\\templates\\module\\default\\template\\windows\\src\\{{moduleIdAsIdentifier}  [DEBUG] Copying C:\\ProgramData\\Titanium\\mobilesdk\\win32\\5.4.0.v20160627224205\\windows\\templates\\module\\default\\template\\windows\\test\\CMakeLists.txt.ejs =>  [DEBUG] Copying C:\\ProgramData\\Titanium\\mobilesdk\\win32\\5.4.0.v20160627224205\\windows\\templates\\module\\default\\template\\windows\\timodule.xml => C:\\Users\\te  [INFO]  Copying CMake package finders  [INFO]  Skipping WindowsPhone ARM project as Windows 8.1 SDK is not installed  [INFO]  Skipping WindowsPhone Win32 project as Windows 8.1 SDK is not installed  [INFO]  Skipping WindowsStore Win3 project as Windows 8.1 SDK is not installed  [INFO]  Generating Windows 10 Win32 project  [INFO]  Generating solution under vsbuild directory to avoid path length issues...  [INFO]  -- The C compiler identification is MSVC 19.0.24210.0  [INFO]  -- The CXX compiler identification is MSVC 19.0.24210.0  [INFO]  -- Check for working C compiler using: Visual Studio 14 2015  [INFO]  -- Check for working C compiler using: Visual Studio 14 2015 -- works  [INFO]  -- Dete